we stand out in-- so developing

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:17.960
features and products faster,
helping you to scale globally,

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:20.002
and efficient pricing.

00:06:20.002 --> 00:06:22.460
Let's start off with feature
and product development first.

00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:27.770
Let's talk about MainAd.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:30.145
I'm actually going to talk
through some customer examples

00:06:30.145 --> 00:06:32.330
here rather than just talking
about conceptually how

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:33.163
Google can help you.

00:06:33.163 --> 00:06:38.090
So MainAd is a real-time bidding
and programmatic ad retargeting

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:39.190
company.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:42.890
They were originally running
at about 50,000 requests

00:06:42.890 --> 00:06:44.720
per second, but they
recognized that they

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.860
needed to grow faster.

00:06:46.860 --> 00:06:50.570
And in moving to Google
Cloud, the important part

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:53.836
was actually the impact
on their business outcome.

00:06:53.836 --> 00:06:56.210
They were actually able to
improve their bidding accuracy

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:58.220
by 75%.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:01.970
And obviously, being a
performance management company,

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:03.650
a performance
marketing company, that

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:05.150
made a huge difference
to both what

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:07.025
they were able to provide
to their customers,

00:07:07.025 --> 00:07:09.440
and also their own
business outcomes.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:11.870
They launched a new
platform on Google Cloud

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:15.370
and focused on AI
machine learning.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.980
And in doing that,
they were able to apply

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:20.720
real-time predictive
analytics to ad retargeting.

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:24.950
And again, very, very
significant impact on their

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:29.000
conversions, which is a big part
of their business, a big part

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:31.670
of their growth, and
how to make money

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:33.770
for themselves and
for their customers.

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:38.175
In terms of scaling globally, I
have, on a number of occasions,

00:07:38.175 --> 00:07:40.550
actually shared this data with
Dan from Infectious Media.

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:43.460
And I think his story
is pretty fantastic.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.610
He pretty gleefully
talks about the fact

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:49.760
that he originally built the
technology infrastructure

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:55.550
on a different cloud and
then just could not scale,

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:59.180
and actually made the decision
that I haven't come across,

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:01.640
actually, that I'll
just asked the audience.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:04.730
He actually moved from
Cloud back to on prem

00:08:04.730 --> 00:08:07.490
in order to be able to deal with
some of the performance issues

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:08.073
he was seeing.

00:08:08.073 --> 00:08:10.360
And I'm just asking, has
anyone else done that?

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:12.110
Have you moved from
Cloud back to on prem?

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:16.765
It's not a direction we
see a lot of people go.

00:08:16.765 --> 00:08:19.870
Oh, OK.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:21.969
He explained the logic
of it in terms of he

00:08:21.969 --> 00:08:23.760
did actually solve his
performance problem,

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:24.950
but all that happened
was that he then

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:26.390
had a gigantic scaling problem.

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:29.810
The scaling problem was that his
costs started scaling linearly

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:31.230
back when he was on prem.

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:34.370
So he actually hit a point
where they really wanted

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:37.010
to launch in APAC, in Asia.

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:39.260
And they knew that was going
to be a huge, huge growth

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:40.400
in their business.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.858
They were caught in this dilemma
of whether they were going

00:08:42.858 --> 00:08:46.670
to launch on prem and then
migrate to Google Cloud,

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:49.874
or whether they would
actually move to Google Cloud

00:08:49.874 --> 00:08:50.540
and then launch.

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:52.748
But they knew that there
was a huge amount of revenue

00:08:52.748 --> 00:08:56.554
and business that they'd lose if
they either made a mess of it,

00:08:56.554 --> 00:08:57.720
or if they delayed too long.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.095
So we were able to convince
them that they could actually

00:09:00.095 --> 00:09:02.760
do both in a very, very
short period of time.

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:07.350
And it went very,
very well for them.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.990
They actually migrated their
entire business in a week

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:13.380
with no downtime,
then launched in APAC,

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:15.820
which quadrupled their business.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:18.030
And one of the most
amazing stats about that

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:21.700
is that at 4x the size--

00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.300
so they went from 35,000
transactions per second

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:27.840
to four times that
after launch in APAC--

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.399
their cost base
remained the same

00:09:29.399 --> 00:09:30.940
compared to what
they'd been on prem.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:32.314
So they were
absolutely delighted

00:09:32.314 --> 00:09:36.270
with both the performance,
the scalability, and the cost.

00:09:36.270 --> 00:09:38.205
So actually, and
that's the next area

00:09:38.205 --> 00:09:40.080
that I want to talk
about, efficient pricing.

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:46.910
So moving to the cloud is
not all about saving money.

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:48.660
But we do recognize
that efficient pricing

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:53.925
is a very, very important
part of your business model.

00:09:53.925 --> 00:09:56.130
And we want to think
of it in terms of,

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:58.020
by providing efficient
pricing that you only

00:09:58.020 --> 00:10:00.478
pay for what you use, that
gives you more resource that you

00:10:00.478 --> 00:10:05.070
can reinvest in your business
and reinvest in growth.

00:10:05.070 --> 00:10:09.480
So Knorex, also a programmatic
advertising platform,

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:13.014
also totally focused on
scalability and speed,

00:10:13.014 --> 00:10:15.180
and they wanted to build
out their real-time bidding

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:19.740
functionality powered
by machine learning.

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.030
Here, they did.

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:23.700
They moved across, and they
got an immediate 30% reduction

00:10:23.700 --> 00:10:26.970
in cost, which they were
then able to reinvest

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:28.415
in the growth of their business.

00:10:28.415 --> 00:10:32.360
They actually said that,
although that was great,

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:34.770
that one-time cost
reduction was fantastic,

00:10:34.770 --> 00:10:37.980
what they appreciated even
more was their freeing up

00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:41.190
their precious developer
resources from doing

00:10:41.190 --> 00:10:43.290
operational tasks and
getting them to actually

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:46.230
be able to develop the tools
and the technologies that

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:47.730
were actually going
to drive growth

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:49.176
and revenue for their business.

00:10:49.176 --> 00:10:50.550
So it's the
combination, I think,

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:53.227
of the freeing of resources that
losing the opportunity costs.

00:10:53.227 --> 00:10:55.560
And then, of course, there
is a cost-benefit, obviously,

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:58.120
of moving to the cloud.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.120
So what does this mean
for your business?

00:11:00.120 --> 00:11:04.720
So we've built our cloud
to be hyper-efficient,

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.620
very security conscious,
scalable for ourselves.

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:10.020
And we now want to
bring that to you

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:12.480
and help you transform
the way you can build

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.301
your own marketing technology.

00:11:14.301 --> 00:11:16.800
So at this stage, I'd like to
invoice my good friend, Sudhir

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:20.520
Hasbe, who's the PM director
for data analytics to the stage,

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:23.490
to go even deeper
on what we can do

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:27.185
to help you to build a top
notch marketing technology.

00:11:27.185 --> 00:11:27.810
Thanks, Sudhir.

